---
// Implement Check: a bookmark run on a client's page compares the HTML the server sends with the page as shown,
// and sends the result here, one row per page type. Spec: private\implement-check\SPEC.md (agreed 2026-11-10).
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import TopBar from "../../components/TopBar.astro";
import { v, importmap } from "../../lib/v.mjs";
---
<Page
  title="Implement Check: Where a Page’s Content and SEO Tags Come From | jsal.io"
  description="Before editing a client’s site, check each page type: is the title, description, H1, canonical, schema and content in the HTML, or added by JavaScript? Free, in your browser."
  path="/implement-check/"
  ogDescription="Check each page type of a client’s site before you edit it: what’s in the HTML, what JavaScript adds or changes, and which template and cache are in the way."
  ogImage="implement-check"
  ogImageAlt="Implement Check: where a page’s content and SEO tags really come from"
  icon="/img/icons/implement-check.svg"
  mono={false}
>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "Implement Check",
    "url": "https://jsal.io/implement-check/",
    "description": "A bookmark that checks a page on any site: whether its title, description, H1, canonical, robots, schema, share tags, hreflang and content are in the HTML the server sends or added or changed by JavaScript, which platform, template and page builder made it, and whether a cache is serving an older copy. Results gather in a sheet by page type. Runs entirely in the browser.",
    "dateModified": "2026-11-10",
    "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "Any (web browser)",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" },
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://jsal.io/#john", "name": "John Salvador", "url": "https://jsal.io/" },
    "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://jsal.io/#website" }
  }
  </script>
<link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href={v("styles.css", "/implement-check/")}>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="importmap" set:html={importmap("/implement-check/", ["./js/app.js"])}></script>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="module" src={v("js/app.js", "/implement-check/")}></script>
  <main class="app" data-bookmarklet={v("js/bookmarklet.js", "/implement-check/")}>

    <!-- Top bar shared by every jsal.io app (styles in /shell.css; the logo menu and theme button come from /nav.js) -->
    <TopBar class="app-header"><h1 slot="title" class="jsal-title"><img class="jsal-title-ico" src={v("/img/icons/implement-check.svg")} alt="" width="22" height="22">Implement <span class="hl">Check</span><span class="sr-only">: where a page’s content and SEO tags come from</span></h1>
<a class="jsal-link" href="#about">About</a></TopBar>
    <p class="jsal-for">For anyone editing pages on a client site: see where each page type’s content and tags really come from.</p>

    <!-- The bookmark: dragged to the bookmarks bar, then clicked on the client's pages -->
    <div class="install">
      <a class="bm" id="bm" href="#about" draggable="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18.6 12.6V8.3H9.4v15.4h5.2M12.2 12.2h3.5M12.2 15.9h1.8M23.1 18.9a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-7 0 3.5 3.5 0 1 1 7 0zM21.9 21.5l2.6 2.6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Implement Check</a>
      <p class="install-how"><strong>Drag this to your bookmarks bar.</strong> Then open one page of each type on the client’s site, click the bookmark, and press Send to sheet. <span class="install-bar">No bookmarks bar? Press <kbd class="mod-key">Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>B</kbd>.</span></p>
      <p class="install-tap" id="bmTap" role="status" hidden>Drag it to the bookmarks bar rather than clicking it here: it checks the page you’re on.</p>
      <p class="install-desk">The bookmark works in desktop browsers. Open this page on a computer to use it.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="work" aria-label="Page types">
      <div class="types">
        <ul class="type-list" id="types"></ul>
        <form class="add" id="addForm" hidden><input type="text" id="addName" maxlength="40" placeholder="Page type, e.g. Location page" aria-label="New page type"><button type="submit" class="jsal-btn small">Add</button></form>
        <p class="type-tools"><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="addBtn">Add a page type</button><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="copySheet">Copy sheet</button><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link danger" id="clearBtn">Clear</button><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="undoClear" hidden>Undo clear</button></p>
        <p class="privacy">Results stay in this browser. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="detail" id="detail" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Fragment set:html={`<!-- About: below the app (which fills the first screen); styles in /shell.css -->`} />
  <section class="jsal-about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
    <h2 id="about-h">About Implement Check</h2>
    <p class="jsal-lead">Before you edit a client’s pages, find out what really makes each one: the CMS field, a custom template, a page builder, a script or a cache.</p>

    <h3>How to use it</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Drag the <strong>Implement Check</strong> button above to your bookmarks bar.</li>
      <li>On the client’s site, open one page of a type you’ll edit (the home page, a blog post, a product, a collection…) and click the bookmark. A panel opens on the page.</li>
      <li>Read each line: <strong>In the HTML</strong> is what search engines get straight away; <strong>Added by JavaScript</strong> and <strong>Changed by JavaScript</strong> mean something other than the page’s own HTML sets it.</li>
      <li>To see whether a CMS field is used, paste its text into <strong>Find</strong>. Not found means this template ignores that field.</li>
      <li>Press <strong>Send to sheet</strong>. Each page type gets a row here, with room for your notes on how to implement, and <strong>Copy sheet</strong> pastes it all into a spreadsheet.</li>
    </ol>

    <details>
      <summary><h3>What it checks</h3></summary>
      <ul>
        <li>The title and meta description (with their lengths), the H1s, the canonical (and whether it points to the page itself), meta robots and the X-Robots-Tag header.</li>
        <li>Schema (JSON-LD): which types, any block that won’t parse, and types added twice, as when a theme and a plugin both add them.</li>
        <li>The share tags (og:title, og:description, og:image) and hreflang.</li>
        <li>How much text the server sends against how much the page shows.</li>
        <li>The platform, template and page builder, and the SEO plugin on WordPress, where the page says so.</li>
        <li>The cache: whether visitors get a cached copy, how old it is, any caching plugin, and whether that copy is older than a fresh one.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <h3>Common questions</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Does it send the client’s pages anywhere?</dt>
      <dd>No. The bookmark reads the page in your browser and fetches it once more from the same site; the result comes here after the # in the address, which browsers never send to a server. The sheet is kept in this browser only.</dd>
      <dt>Why “Added by JavaScript” if Google runs JavaScript?</dt>
      <dd>Google does render pages, but later and not always; other search engines, AI crawlers and share previews often don’t. More to the point for editing: if a script sets the title, changing the CMS field may do nothing.</dd>
      <dt>Why does a line say the cache is older?</dt>
      <dd>Visitors are getting a saved copy from before the latest change. Clear the site’s cache (its plugin, host or CDN) after saving, then check again.</dd>
    </dl>

    <p class="jsal-feedback">Useful? Ideas or problems? <a href="mailto:dev@jsal.io?subject=Implement%20Check">Email me</a>.</p>
    <p><svg class="jsal-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="jsal-mark-tile" x=".5" y=".5" width="31" height="31" rx="6.5"/><path class="jsal-mark-j" d="M20 15V20a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-9 0"/><path class="jsal-mark-gem" d="M20 5l3 3-3 3-3-3z"/></svg>Made by <a href="/">John Salvador</a>. Also try <a href="/cms-picker/">CMS Picker</a> to see what each CMS can do, or <a href="/formatter/">Clean Paste</a> to clean up content before it goes in. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Page>
